Sval: the Windows installer keeps to Sval's own registry keys and files

Firefox and Sval run side by side without touching each other's state.
Mozilla's installer writes several names that are Firefox's whatever the
application's identity:

- AppName was "Firefox", so the installer kept the taskbar ids, the
  32-to-64-bit migration flag, the installer's prefs and the default
  agent's shortcut under Software\Mozilla\Firefox, where Firefox's
  WindowsInstallsInfo counts installs and where Sval itself reads
  Software\Mozilla\Sval (WinTaskbar, UpdateService). AppName is the
  application's name, as application.ini has it.
- The uninstaller left Uninstalled-<channel> in Software\Mozilla\Firefox,
  which BrowserGlue reads and deletes at startup, so uninstalling one app
  offered the other a reset. Both use the application's own key.
- The launcher process's key is SOFTWARE\<vendor>\<name>\Launcher
  (LauncherRegistryInfo::kLauncherSubKeyPath); the installer wrote and
  cleaned Software\Mozilla\Firefox\Launcher.
- The installer and every update wrote the legacy
  Software\mozilla.org\Mozilla CurrentVersion that Firefox also writes, and
  moved or deleted %LOCALAPPDATA%\Mozilla\Firefox\postSigningData, which is
  Firefox's.
- App Paths is keyed by the executable's name, firefox.exe, so installing
  Sval made "firefox" in Run start Sval, and uninstalling it with no other
  Sval left removed the key whoever held it. Sval takes the key only when
  no other install holds it, and removes it only when it is its own.

browser/installer/windows/moz.build passes the application's name and
vendor to defines.nsi.in.

diff --git a/browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs b/browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs
index d73aed7..6729104 100644
--- a/browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs
@@ -837,12 +837,12 @@ BrowserGlue.prototype = {
       if (updateChannel) {
         let uninstalledValue = lazy.WindowsRegistry.readRegKey(
           Ci.nsIWindowsRegKey.ROOT_KEY_CURRENT_USER,
-          "Software\\Mozilla\\Firefox",
+          `Software\\Mozilla\\${Services.appinfo.name}`,
           `Uninstalled-${updateChannel}`
         );
         let removalSuccessful = lazy.WindowsRegistry.removeRegKey(
           Ci.nsIWindowsRegKey.ROOT_KEY_CURRENT_USER,
-          "Software\\Mozilla\\Firefox",
+          `Software\\Mozilla\\${Services.appinfo.name}`,
           `Uninstalled-${updateChannel}`
         );
         if (removalSuccessful && uninstalledValue == "True") {
